Who benefits when a neighborhood becomes more desirable because of the activities of its occupants? Can the tenants and institutions that create that value share in it? What can they do to stay? Must they keep moving as neighborhoods become more expensive? Should they become more institutionalized? How can new cultural spaces still emerge?

{% figura src="/images/vignettes/julia-12.jpg" alt="A map of Lower Manhattan tracing the moves of The Loft from 1975 to 2001, with a note on why each move happened" /%}
